        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 30–32; described as overweight"
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral knee pain"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Longstanding dull ache in the medial and anterior knees. Worse with walking more than 10–15 minutes, stairs, and prolonged standing; eased by rest and sitting. Occasional night pain, not waking the patient most nights."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral knee stiffness"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Stiff after sitting for more than 20–30 minutes and on waking; loosens after a few minutes of moving."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral knee instability and near falls"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent subjective giving way in both knees for approximately 6–9 months, right worse than left, especially when going down steps or getting up from a chair. Reports 3–4 near falls in the last 2 months, with no definite complete fall or head strike. Feels knees are wobbly and may buckle. No episodes of giving way with sharp severe pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral knee swelling"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports knees become puffy at the end of the day. No redness or warmth reported."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Bilateral knee crepitus"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports marked, persistent cracking and grinding."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Knee locking"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient denies true locking."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Knee gait and mobility"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Slight antalgic gait, short stride and slow pace; cautious turning and mild varus knees. No walking aid."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Knee examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild bilateral bony enlargement and slight varus; small effusions in both knees, right greater than left. Mild bilateral medial joint-line tenderness. No erythema or warmth. No obvious ligament laxity with valgus or varus stress at 0° or 30°. Flexion to approximately 110° with end-range pain; extension near full. Marked crepitus through range of motion. McMurray negative for click or locking, with some medial discomfort only. No posterior tenderness or calf swelling."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Hand symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Intermittent hand pain and stiffness, especially in the DIP and PIP joints with heavy use. Reports bony nodules at the fingertips; no acute flare today."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Hand examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Several Heberden nodes at DIP joints and some PIP nodes; mild tenderness. No synovial thickening or warmth. Range of motion preserved with slight end-range discomfort."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-18",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Lower limb neurological examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Power 5/5 in major muscle groups; light-touch sensation intact; reflexes normal; no focal deficit."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-19",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-19",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Neurological and cardiopulmonary symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies dizziness, syncope, chest pain, palpitations, new neurological symptoms, peripheral paraesthesia, or focal weakness apart from subjective wobbly knees."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-20",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-20",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Systemic and inflammatory symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies fevers, weight loss, night sweats, rash, eye inflammation, inflammatory back pain, recent infection, or other systemic symptoms."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-21",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-21",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Spinal red-flag symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies bowel or bladder incontinence and saddle anaesthesia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-22",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-22",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and behaviour"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mobile but cautious and mildly irritable; frequently challenged explanations. Hostile tone at times, but remained in the room and answered focused questions."
      }
    },
